  [allowed] probes/tape/bios_probe_tapraw.py — ✅ ARCHIVED AND RE-PROVED END TO END 2026-08-31 (D-CASINSETTLE), on the Philips_VG_8020: minted, booted under openMSX, result buffer read back. R14 half-periods ~4 iterations off a synthesised .cas and ~14 off a 1200-baud WAV -- a 3.5x ratio against the 3744/1200 = 3.1x the two encodings imply. It was ALSO the GREEN CONTROL that convicted bios_probe_casin: it blocks on edges instead of counting down, so it reads the very signal casin's settle window was missing.
  [allowed] probes/tape/bios_probe_tapread.py — ✅ ARCHIVED AND RE-PROVED END TO END 2026-09-01 (D-TAPPAIR): paired with bios_probe_tapwrite on the VG-8020 -- write cart recorded to WAV (--record), read cart booted on that WAV (--cassette), all six PATTERN bytes byte-identical, TAPION locked, carries 00. The recipe: tapwrite --out w.rom; omsx_run --record rec.wav --bp 0x7FF0; tapread --out r.rom; omsx_run --cassette rec.wav --mem memory:0xE000:8; tapread --analyze. The 2026-08-31 entry called this pairing a job, not a rot -- it was, and it took five commands.
